                       "text":  "Psalm 15 The Righteous Israelite - A psalm of David. I - LORD, who may abide in your tent? Who may dwell on your holy mountain?",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "2",
                       "number":  2,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "II - Whoever walks without blame, doing what is right, speaking truth from the heart;",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "3",
                       "number":  3,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Who does not slander with his tongue, does no harm to a friend, never defames a neighbor;",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "4",
                       "number":  4,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Who disdains the wicked, but honors those who fear the LORD; Who keeps an oath despite the cost,",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "5",
                       "number":  5,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "lends no money at interest, accepts no bribe against the innocent. III - Whoever acts like this shall never be shaken.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   }
               ],
